<main class="section"><div class="container legal"><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p><strong>Effective September 7, 2026</strong></p><p>CajunSites respects your privacy. This policy explains what information we collect through cajunsites.com, how we use it, and the choices available to you.</p><h2>Information we collect</h2><p>When you contact us or submit our Get Started form, we may collect information such as your name, business name, email address, phone number, business type, domain information, services, and other information you choose to provide.</p><p>Our website also uses Cloudflare Turnstile to help protect forms from automated abuse. Cloudflare may process information necessary to provide that security service.</p><h2>How we use information</h2><p>We use information you submit to respond to inquiries, evaluate website projects, communicate with you, provide requested services, maintain customer relationships, and operate and improve CajunSites.</p><h2>Service providers</h2><p>We use third-party service providers to operate portions of our website and business, including hosting, security, email delivery, billing, and related services. These providers may process information only as reasonably necessary to provide their services.</p><h2>Information sharing</h2><p>We do not sell your personal information. We may disclose information when necessary to provide requested services, comply with applicable law, protect our rights, or prevent fraud, abuse, or security threats.</p><h2>Data retention</h2><p>We retain submitted information for as long as reasonably necessary to respond to inquiries, provide services, maintain business records, resolve disputes, and meet legal or operational requirements.</p><h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2><p>CajunSites may use cookies or similar technologies required for website functionality, security, analytics, or other legitimate operational purposes. Third-party services may use their own technologies subject to their respective policies.</p><h2>Your choices</h2><p>You may contact us to ask about the personal information we maintain about you or to request correction of inaccurate information, subject to applicable legal and operational requirements.</p><h2>Children</h2><p>CajunSites is a business service and is not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children through this website.</p><h2>Changes to this policy</h2><p>We may update this policy from time to time. The effective date above indicates when the current version took effect.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>Privacy questions or requests can be sent to <a href="mailto:hello@cajunsites.com">hello@cajunsites.com</a>.</p></div></main>
